.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-offbox 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-offbox \- Keep this session\*(Aqs state in a repository off this machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten offbox\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Keep this session\*(Aqs state in a repository off this machine
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-offbox\-status(1)
Whether the state repository the environment names can be written from here
.TP
batten\-offbox\-push(1)
Snapshot one session and make it the value of its ref on the state repository
.TP
batten\-offbox\-restore(1)
Put a session\*(Aqs pushed snapshot back where it was read from, in a container that does not have it
.TP
batten\-offbox\-run(1)
Run this session\*(Aqs off\-box daemon until it is killed: push when there is something new, wait when the forge says to
.TP
batten\-offbox\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
